  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Control",
      "items": [
        "The app launches click and macro workers on daemon threads. (autoclicker/app.py:63–105)",
        "Pynput listens for global hotkeys and captured mouse/keyboard events, then routes them to app callbacks. (autoclicker/app.py:42–52, 141–191, 814–817)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Execution",
      "items": [
        "Shared runtime state holds running and recording flags, counters, macro events, and multipoint targets. (autoclicker/state.py:3–10)",
        "PyAutoGUI pointer-corner failsafe is enabled. (autoclicker/dependencies.py:16–20; README.md:17)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Local data",
      "items": [
        "Settings are saved in ~/.autoclicker_config.json; macro JSON is selected by the user. (autoclicker/config.py:3–5; autoclicker/app.py:211–235, 265–310)",
        "Recorded macros can contain key presses and screen coordinates, so review files before sharing them. (README.md:40–42; autoclicker/app.py:149–180, 211–235)"
      ]
    }
  ]
